ENTRY            22766   20230213   20230523   20230504       2314
SUBENT        22766001   20230213   20230523   20230504       2314
BIB                 13         53
TITLE      Double and single differential neutron emission cross
            sections at 14.1 MeV for natFe, 16O and and natNi
AUTHOR     (A.Takahashi, M.Gotoh, Y.Sasaki, H.Sugimoto)
INSTITUTE  (2JPNOSA)
REFERENCE  (R,OKTAV-A-92-01,1992)
REL-REF    (O,22106001,A.Takahashi+,R,OKTAV-A-92-01,1992)
            Bi data sets
           (O,22136001,A.Takahashi+,R,OKTAV-A-92-01,1992)
            Nb and Ta data sets
           (O,22186001,A.Takahashi+,R,OKTAV-A-92-01,1992)
            Sb data sets
FACILITY   (CCW,2JPNOSA) Intense 14 MeV neutron source OKTAVIAN
INC-SOURCE (D-T) 2 cm in diameter tritium target. Less than 2 ns
            pulsed neutrons were generated
METHOD     (TOF) Flight path of ~8.3 m fixed at 85 deg.
           (PSD) Two parallel pulse shape discrimination circuits
            for separation of neutron signals from gamma signals.
DETECTOR   (SCIN ) NE-213 liquid scintillator (25.4 cm in diam.,
             10 cm in length).
            The other NE-213 scintillator (5.08 cm diam., 5.08 cm
             in length) for source neutron flux was monitor at
             0 deg against the deuteron beam line.
SAMPLE      Cylindrical samples of different sizes.
CORRECTION  Corrections are made for
             - multiple scattering;
             - attenuation;
             - neutron source contamination.
             with the help of MUSCC3 code based on JENDL-3.
            In case that JENDL-3 would produce double
             differential neutron emission spectrum in drastic
             disagreement with the measured one, the correction
             can be skipped and the adoption of raw (i.e.
             experimental) data is recommended by authors.
            This correction amounted to about 10% except for
             backward elastic scattering where it could be up to
             30%.
COMMENT    By authors:
            Correction factor are calculated using evaluated data,
             however, they are still primitive.
            Calculation of correction factors should be carried
             out again after new version of evaluation would be
             published.
HISTORY    (20030820C) VM + SD
           (20041122U) CORRECTED, SM
           (20090406A) For Fe-nat, Ni-nat and O-16 re-compiled
            with the usage of full data sets given in main
            reference. Data for Bi-209, Nb-93, Sb-nat moved to
            existing ENTRIES: 22106, 22136, 22186 - S.M.
           (20161130A) On. 004-007 deleted. Same data in 22106,
            22136 or 22186.
           (20170824A) SD: Subents 008,025,031 deleted (see
            MEMO 4C-3/408).
           (20230213A) SD: Correction in Subent 011.
ENDBIB              53
